WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:01.620
Good morning, John.

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:05.200
I know, I'm too late, I don't know what I'm thinking,

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.860
I'm on the wrong side of the Bell Curve, I'm catching the wave as it crashes but

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.480
I simply ... cannot ... help myself.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:13.420
[Music: Do The Harlem-]

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:30.040
[Music: Promise - Komi Hirose]

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:35.260
[Music: Dragostea din tei (aka Numa Numa) by O-Zone]

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:43.720
[Music: Gangnam Style - PSY]

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:47.260
[Music: Promise - Komi Hirose]

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:51.140
I guess... I'm a little bit of an Internet dance craze hipster, it turns out

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:53.640
I mean, yeah, it's great, Harlem Shake,

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:56.000
but don't forget about Gadan, people

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:59.220
Its feelings might get hurt, and Numa Numa? C'mon!

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:03.420
Alright, because I can't help but not think too much about... everything.

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:09.600
I am really curious as to why internet dance craze videos often... seem to be bilingual.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:10.480
English and Spanish.

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:11.520
English and Japanese

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:12.580
English and Korean

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:13.860
English and Moldovan

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:15.980
English and ... Soldier Boy.

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:19.640
Of course, it is important to note that this trend pre-dates internet culture.

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:25.000
And also it is still completely possible in the Internet Age to have a dance craze based on a unilingual song.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:30.480
But it is definitely a majority and it is definitely a trend, and I definitely don't know why.. it is...

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:34.320
... though I have some little guesses but they're not good enough for the light of day, I don't think.

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:36.280
So. Ideas? ... comments.... help.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:39.980
Alright, enough of that. You people are probably waiting for me to talk about something else.

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:42.560
I'm kind of avoiding it, 'cause it's freaking me out.

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:46.240
It has been a big week in ... [Hank does mouth sounds]

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:52.980
John. You, my brother, John got to interview the President a bit. Which was cooool.

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:53.760
Here's a highlight:

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:59.220
[John]: Almost all economists agree that we should stop minting pennies. It's a really obvious thing...

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:03.560
... it's not a particularly interesting or partisan thing, but it's really obvious.

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:05.300
So my question to you is why haven't we done it?

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:10.580
[Pres. Obama]: You know, I gotta tell you, John, I don't know. [stumbles for words]

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:15.560
It's one of those things where I think people get attached emotionally to the way things have been.

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:19.340
[Hank]: John Green - you stumped the President... Pretty cool.

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:22.440
But in addition to that, The Brain Scoop was featured on NPR.

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:25.060
Wheezy Waiter and Shay Carl got to make a video with Matt Damon who ...

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:26.540
... you may or may not know is my idol.

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:31.720
Lizzie Bennett Diaries won two Streamies. These are the pre-awards. We may still yet win more.

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:34.160
And we launched Crash Course: Chemistry, which I'm very excited about.

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:36.720
And I got back from the United Kingdom, so I don't really know what time it is.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:42.160
And... oh yeah. Also, the President refused to name your unborn child.

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:48.020
[Pres. Obama]: If I gave a preference and you guys went the other way, forever this child would say...

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:49.700
... "The President doesn't like my name".

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:55.000
The main thing is tell either Eleanor or Alice to not to forget to be awesome.

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:56.500
[Hank]: What?!

00:02:56.500 --> 00:03:01.320
[Hank makes more mouth sounds while a Harlem Shake/mix song gradually fades in]

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:13.960
[Dance music mashup by Maxton]

